## Prior art — algorithms re-implemented from published papers

Named here, and only here, because a citation is not a dependency. In each case the equations from the
paper were implemented in pure numpy; no code was copied and no dataset or checkpoint from these projects
is used, fetched, or required at any point.

Dex-Net 3.0 (Mahler et al., ICRA 2018) — the analytic vacuum/wrench model that
  src/robot/grasping/suction/wrench.py implements from the paper's statics.
SuctionNet-1Billion (Cao et al., RA-L 2021) and Sim-Suction — the deformable-cup seal formulation that
  src/robot/grasping/suction/seal.py implements as concentric ring sampling.

Their DATASETS and PRETRAINED WEIGHTS are non-commercial (GraspNet-1Billion: CC BY-NC-SA) and are
therefore out of bounds for this project — see tests/test_license_boundary.py.


## Asset licensing rule

Meshes, textures and generated scenes may use CC0, CC-BY, or assets we produce ourselves — never a
non-commercial licence, and never a research-only dataset. Enforced by
tests/test_license_boundary.py::audit_asset_rows once the scene generator emits its first manifest.
